eq r\}. So only terms belonging to classes k′≠kk^{\prime}
eq k appear in the denominator of (3). CorrSynth Intra-label: When generating a sequence for class kk and m=(k−1)​R+rm=(k-1)R+r, we set γm,n=0\gamma_{m,n}=0 for n∈{(k′−1)R+r′:r′∈[R],k′≠k}n\in\{(k^{\prime}-1)R+r^{\prime}:r^{\prime}\in[R],k^{\prime}
